The old 2x2 grid of Receitas/Despesas/Investimentos/Saldo made you read
all four numbers to understand the month. Replaced it with a MonthFlow
component: o saldo leads as the one number that matters day-to-day,
with a single bar underneath showing despesas vs. investimentos scaled
against receitas (or against their own total when spending+investing
exceeds income, so the bar can never overflow its track), plus a small
legend with the exact values.

Checked the three edge cases that matter for a bar like this — a normal
positive-balance month, a month where expenses+investments exceed
income (segments correctly cap at 100% instead of overflowing), and a
zero-activity month (empty track, no stray legend items) — via a static
mockup with the exact classes/computed widths before wiring it into the
real component.

